Derived from the author's private Agent Platform Next:
- the audit-trail concept (separate writer, peer attribution, hash chain with signatures,
  external anchors, gap markers, ALCOA+ mapping), which was planned there but never built and
  is implemented here;
- the session-format knowledge of its native history readers for Claude Code, Codex and pi
  (identity rules, record types, safe file reading), adapted and reduced to what evidence
  records need.
No private paths, hosts, names or data were copied. All test fixtures are synthetic.

Runtime dependencies: aqt-spec (Apache-2.0), cryptography (Apache-2.0 OR BSD-3-Clause).
Test-only: pytest (MIT), jsonschema (MIT).
Ideas only, no code: RFC 3161 time-stamp handling as practised by eLabFTW (AGPL) and
`openssl ts`; C2SP checkpoint and Rekor v2 log/TSA split (Apache-2.0).
